    question: "What is Java and its main features?",
    idealAnswer: "**Java**: A high-level, object-oriented programming language developed by Sun Microsystems (now Oracle) in 1995.\n\n**Main Features**:\n\n**1. Platform Independent (WORA)**:\n```java\n// Same .class file runs on any platform with JVM\n// Compiled on Windows, runs on Mac, Linux, etc.\npublic class HelloWorld {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        System.out.println(\"Hello, World!\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**2. Object-Oriented**:\n```java\n// Everything is an object (except primitives)\npublic class Car {\n    private String model;\n    \n    public Car(String model) {\n        this.model = model;\n    }\n    \n    public void drive() {\n        System.out.println(\"Driving \" + model);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**3. Simple & Secure**:\n- No pointer arithmetic (unlike C/C++)\n- Automatic memory management (Garbage Collection)\n- Built-in security manager and sandbox\n\n**4. Robust & Multithreaded**:\n```java\n// Exception handling makes code robust\ntry {\n    int result = 10 / 0;\n} catch (ArithmeticException e) {\n    System.out.println(\"Cannot divide by zero\");\n}\n\n// Built-in multithreading support\nThread thread = new Thread(() -> {\n    System.out.println(\"Running in separate thread\");\n});\nthread.start();\n```\n\n**5. High Performance**:\n- Just-In-Time (JIT) compiler\n- Automatic optimization\n\n**6. Distributed**:\n- RMI (Remote Method Invocation)\n- Socket programming support",
