    category: "OOP Concepts",
    question: "What is inheritance in Java?",
    idealAnswer: "**Inheritance**: Mechanism where a child class acquires properties of parent class.\n\n**1. Basic Inheritance Example**:\n```java\n// Parent class (superclass)\nclass Vehicle {\n    protected String brand;\n    protected int year;\n    protected boolean isRunning;\n    \n    public Vehicle(String brand, int year) {\n        this.brand = brand;\n        this.year = year;\n        this.isRunning = false;\n    }\n    \n    public void start() {\n        isRunning = true;\n        System.out.println(brand + \" vehicle started\");\n    }\n    \n    public void stop() {\n        isRunning = false;\n        System.out.println(brand + \" vehicle stopped\");\n    }\n    \n    public void displayInfo() {\n        System.out.println(\"Brand: \" + brand + \", Year: \" + year);\n    }\n    \n    // Getters\n    public String getBrand() { return brand; }\n    public int getYear() { return year; }\n    public boolean isRunning() { return isRunning; }\n}\n\n// Child class (subclass)\nclass Car extends Vehicle {\n    private int numberOfDoors;\n    private String fuelType;\n    \n    public Car(String brand, int year, int doors, String fuel) {\n        super(brand, year);  // Call parent constructor\n        this.numberOfDoors = doors;\n        this.fuelType = fuel;\n    }\n    \n    // Method overriding (specific to Car)\n    @Override\n    public void start() {\n        System.out.println(\"Car engine starting with \" + fuelType);\n        isRunning = true;  // Access protected field\n    }\n    \n    // New method specific to Car\n    public void openTrunk() {\n        System.out.println(\"Opening \" + numberOfDoors + \"-door car trunk\");\n    }\n    \n    // Override and extend parent method\n    @Override\n    public void displayInfo() {\n        super.displayInfo();  // Call parent method\n        System.out.println(\"Doors: \" + numberOfDoors + \", Fuel: \" + fuelType);\n    }\n}\n\n// Another child class\nclass Motorcycle extends Vehicle {\n    private boolean hasSidecar;\n    \n    public Motorcycle(String brand, int year, boolean sidecar) {\n        super(brand, year);\n        this.hasSidecar = sidecar;\n    }\n    \n    @Override\n    public void start() {\n        System.out.println(\"Motorcycle engine roaring!\");\n        isRunning = true;\n    }\n    \n    public void doWheelie() {\n        if (isRunning) {\n            System.out.println(\"Doing a wheelie!\");\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(\"Start the motorcycle first!\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**2. Inheritance Usage and Polymorphism**:\n```java\npublic class InheritanceDemo {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        // Create objects of different types\n        Vehicle vehicle = new Vehicle(\"Generic\", 2020);\n        Car car = new Car(\"Toyota\", 2022, 4, \"Gasoline\");\n        Motorcycle motorcycle = new Motorcycle(\"Harley\", 2021, false);\n        \n        // Each object has its own behavior\n        vehicle.start();      // Generic vehicle started\n        car.start();          // Car engine starting with Gasoline\n        motorcycle.start();   // Motorcycle engine roaring!\n        \n        // Access inherited methods\n        car.displayInfo();    // Shows brand, year, doors, fuel\n        motorcycle.displayInfo(); // Shows brand, year\n        \n        // Access specific methods\n        car.openTrunk();      // Car-specific method\n        motorcycle.doWheelie(); // Motorcycle-specific method\n        \n        // Polymorphism - parent reference to child object\n        Vehicle myCar = new Car(\"Honda\", 2023, 2, \"Electric\");\n        Vehicle myBike = new Motorcycle(\"Yamaha\", 2022, true);\n        \n        myCar.start();        // Calls Car's start method (polymorphism)\n        myBike.start();       // Calls Motorcycle's start method\n        \n        // myCar.openTrunk();  // COMPILE ERROR - Vehicle doesn't have this method\n        \n        // Type casting to access specific methods\n        if (myCar instanceof Car) {\n            Car carRef = (Car) myCar;\n            carRef.openTrunk();\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**3. Method Overriding Rules**:\n```java\nclass Parent {\n    public void method1() {\n        System.out.println(\"Parent method1\");\n    }\n    \n    protected void method2() {\n        System.out.println(\"Parent method2\");\n    }\n    \n    // Final method cannot be overridden\n    public final void finalMethod() {\n        System.out.println(\"Cannot override me\");\n    }\n    \n    // Static method cannot be overridden (hidden instead)\n    public static void staticMethod() {\n        System.out.println(\"Parent static method\");\n    }\n}\n\nclass Child extends Parent {\n    @Override\n    public void method1() {\n        System.out.println(\"Child method1\");\n    }\n    \n    @Override\n    protected void method2() {\n        System.out.println(\"Child method2\");\n    }\n    \n    // Cannot override final method\n    // public final void finalMethod() { } // COMPILE ERROR\n    \n    // Hides static method (doesn't override)\n    public static void staticMethod() {\n        System.out.println(\"Child static method\");\n    }\n    \n    // Can change access modifier to more permissive\n    @Override\n    public void method2() {  // Changed from protected to public\n        System.out.println(\"Child method2 with public access\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**4. Constructor Chaining**:\n```java\nclass Grandparent {\n    public Grandparent() {\n        System.out.println(\"Grandparent constructor\");\n    }\n    \n    public Grandparent(String name) {\n        System.out.println(\"Grandparent constructor with name: \" + name);\n    }\n}\n\nclass Parent extends Grandparent {\n    public Parent() {\n        // super() called automatically\n        System.out.println(\"Parent constructor\");\n    }\n    \n    public Parent(String name) {\n        super(name);  // Explicit call to parent constructor\n        System.out.println(\"Parent constructor with name\");\n    }\n}\n\nclass Child extends Parent {\n    public Child() {\n        super(\"Default\");  // Must be first statement\n        System.out.println(\"Child constructor\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**5. Inheritance vs Composition**:\n```java\n// Inheritance (IS-A relationship)\nclass Bird extends Animal {\n    // Bird IS-A Animal\n    void fly() {\n        System.out.println(\"Flying\");\n    }\n}\n\n// Composition (HAS-A relationship)\nclass Car {\n    private Engine engine;  // Car HAS-A Engine\n    private Wheel[] wheels;\n    \n    public Car() {\n        this.engine = new Engine();\n        this.wheels = new Wheel[4];\n    }\n}\n\nclass Engine {\n    void start() {\n        System.out.println(\"Engine starting\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Key Inheritance Concepts**:\n- **Single inheritance**: Java supports only single class inheritance\n- **Multilevel inheritance**: A → B → C chain\n- **Hierarchical inheritance**: One parent, multiple children\n- **Method overriding**: Runtime polymorphism\n- **`super` keyword**: Access parent members\n- **`final` keyword**: Prevent inheritance/overriding\n- **`@Override` annotation**: Compiler check for overriding",
