    idealAnswer: "**Fail-Fast Iterator**:\n- Throws ConcurrentModificationException if collection is modified\n- Works on original collection\n- Doesn't require extra memory\n- Most Java collections (ArrayList, HashMap)\n- Better performance\n\n**Fail-Safe Iterator**:\n- Doesn't throw exception if collection is modified\n- Works on copy of collection\n- Requires extra memory\n- CopyOnWriteArrayList, ConcurrentHashMap\n- Slower performance\n\n**Example**:\n```java\n// Fail-fast - throws exception\nfor(String item : arrayList) {\n  arrayList.add(\"new\"); // ConcurrentModificationException\n}\n\n// Fail-safe - no exception\nfor(String item : copyOnWriteArrayList) {\n  copyOnWriteArrayList.add(\"new\"); // Works fine\n}\n```",
